{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.collatz_no_cycles","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.collatz_no_cycles","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.GeomSum"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.balanced_holonomy_excluded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.balanced_holonomy_excluded","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/collatz_no_cycles.lean#L113-L144","doc":"**Balanced-holonomy cycle exclusion (proved, sorry-free).**\n\nGiven a QOU whose Skein `q`-integers satisfy the Skein divisibility\nrelation `[3]_q = q·[2]_q + 1` with `[2]_q` a non-unit (as holds for\n`[2]_q = q + 1` in the Skein module `ℤ[q^{±1}]`), the equation\n`[3]_q^{k_odd} = [2]_q^{k}` has **no** solution with `k ≥ 1`.\n\nA Skein-Collatz periodic orbit of *balanced* multiplicative holonomy\n(`A = [3]_q^{k_odd}/[2]_q^{k} = 1`) would force exactly this equation,\nso this lemma discharges the `A = 1` sub-case of no-cycles by\ncoprimality — unconditionally, over a generic commutative ring. It\ndoes **not** settle the affine (`A ≠ 1`) case, which is part of the\nopen `conj:q-collatz`.\n\nProof: `[3]_q ≡ 1 (mod [2]_q)` from the divisibility relation, so\n`[2]_q ∣ [3]_q^{k_odd} − 1`; and `[2]_q ∣ [2]_q^{k}` for `k ≥ 1`.\nEquality would give `[2]_q ∣ 1`, i.e. `[2]_q` a unit — contradiction. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:collatz-no-cycles","label":"prop:collatz-no-cycles","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/collatz-no-cycles.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.collatz_no_cycles","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.collatz_no_cycles","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/collatz_no_cycles.lean#L39-L111","doc":"**Manuscript statement** (full body):\n\n**Proposition (balanced-holonomy cycle exclusion, within a QOU).**\nLet $(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)$ be a quantum observable universe with\nsubstrate parameter $q$ and Skein module\n$\\mathcal{S}(q) \\cong \\mathbb{Z}[q^{\\pm 1}]$.\nThe Skein-Collatz map $\\mathcal{C}_q$ has no periodic orbit of balanced\nmultiplicative holonomy ($A = 1$) other than the degenerate fixed point;\nequivalently $[3]_q^{k_{\\mathrm{odd}}} = [2]_q^{k}$ has no solution with\n$k_{\\mathrm{odd}} \\geq 1$, by coprimality of $[2]_q$ and $[3]_q$.\n\n*Proof.* A periodic orbit of length $k$ with $k_{\\mathrm{odd}}$\nodd steps and $k_{\\mathrm{even}}$ even steps satisfies\n$\\mathcal{C}_q^k(P) = P$. The odd steps multiply by\n$[3]_q / [2]_q$ and the even steps multiply by $1/[2]_q$,\nso the return condition requires:\n\n$$\n  \\frac{[3]_q^{k_{\\mathrm{odd}}}}{[2]_q^{k_{\\mathrm{odd}} + k_{\\mathrm{even}}}}\n  =  1,\n  \\qquad\\text{i.e.,}\\qquad\n  [3]_q^{k_{\\mathrm{odd}}} =  [2]_q^k\n  \\quad (k = k_{\\mathrm{odd}} + k_{\\mathrm{even}}).\n$$\n\nBut $[2]_q$ and $[3]_q$ are **coprime** in $\\mathbb{Z}[q]$.\nThe Skein divisibility identity gives the proof in one line:\n\n$$\n  [3]_q - q[2]_q = 1,\n$$\n\nso $\\gcd([2]_q, [3]_q) = 1$ by Bézout.  Since $[3]_q$\nis a unit modulo $[2]_q$:\n\n$$\n  [3]_q^{k_{\\mathrm{odd}}}\n  \\equiv 1^{k_{\\mathrm{odd}}}\n  \\equiv 1\n  \\pmod{[2]_q},\n$$\n\nwhile $[2]_q^k \\equiv 0 \\pmod{[2]_q}$ for $k \\geq 1$.\nThese are never equal for $k_{\\mathrm{odd}} \\geq 1$.\nA cycle with $k_{\\mathrm{odd}} = 0$ (all even steps) would\nbe $P \\mapsto P / [2]_q^k = P$, forcing $P = 0$.\n\nTherefore the only periodic orbit is $P = 1$\n(the unknot).  $\\square$\n\n**Classical limit.** At $q = 1$: $\\gcd(2, 3) = 1$ and\n$3^a \\neq 2^b$ for $a, b > 0$ (unique prime factorization).\nThe $q$-deformation lifts this to polynomial coprimality.\n\n**The full $(a, a+1)$ family.** The identity\n$\\gcd([a]_q, [b]_q) = [\\gcd(a,b)]_q$ shows that all\nCollatz-type maps $(a, a+1)$ exclude periodic cycles,\nsince $\\gcd(a, a+1) = 1$ for all $a$.  Cycle exclusion\nis a consequence of consecutive integers being coprime\n— a fa\n\n[…truncated; see manuscript for remainder…]\n\n    The Lean encoding below states the manuscript claim over a context class and discharges it from the class's fields (§3b-conditional). The declaration type-checks as a complete term; the substantive mathematical content is carried by the context-class axioms, and a full derivation from substrate primitives remains pending. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzNoCyclesContext.no_cycles_of_coprime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzNoCyclesContext.no_cycles_of_coprime","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/collatz_no_cycles.lean#L37-L37","doc":"Manuscript no-cycle claim under the coprime Bézout identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzNoCyclesContext.is_periodic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzNoCyclesContext.is_periodic","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/collatz_no_cycles.lean#L35-L35","doc":"The Skein-Collatz map periodic orbits. The fixed-point set\n`Periodic = {P : ∀ k > 0, C_q^k P ≠ P} ∪ {1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzNoCyclesContext.q_int_3_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzNoCyclesContext.q_int_3_def","kind":"theorem","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/collatz_no_cycles.lean#L32-L32","doc":"Definition of the q-integer 3: `[3]_q = q^2 + q + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzNoCyclesContext.q_int_2_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzNoCyclesContext.q_int_2_def","kind":"theorem","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/collatz_no_cycles.lean#L30-L30","doc":"Definition of the q-integer 2: `[2]_q = q + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzNoCyclesContext.q_int_3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzNoCyclesContext.q_int_3","kind":"def","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/collatz_no_cycles.lean#L28-L28","doc":"The q-integer `[3]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzNoCyclesContext.q_int_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzNoCyclesContext.q_int_2","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/collatz_no_cycles.lean#L26-L26","doc":"The q-integer `[2]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzNoCyclesContext.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzNoCyclesContext.q","kind":"def","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/collatz_no_cycles.lean#L24-L24","doc":"Substrate parameter `q : ℝ` of the QOU. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzNoCyclesContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzNoCyclesContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/collatz_no_cycles.lean#L22-L22","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzNoCyclesContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzNoCyclesContext","kind":"class","line":17,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/collatz_no_cycles.lean#L17-L37","doc":"QOU-furnished context for the `collatz_no_cycles` claim: the fields\nbelow are the Skein data provided by a quantum observable universe\n`(𝐂, A, τ)` — `q` is its substrate parameter and the Skein-Collatz\n`is_periodic` predicate lives on its Skein module. The `_of_coprime`\nfield carries the manuscript no-cycle content conditionally. ","signatureChunk":0}]}